WEBVTT

00:01:26.871 --> 00:01:30.329
was distributed across
different sets of computers

00:01:30.371 --> 00:01:32.621
which mushroomed at CERN.

00:01:32.663 --> 00:01:36.246
Each set was joined together
in dedicated homegrown networks.

00:01:36.288 --> 00:01:40.204
But physicists collaborated without regard
for the boundaries between sets,

00:01:40.246 --> 00:01:42.913
hence needed to access data
on all of these.

00:01:42.954 --> 00:01:47.496
So, we bridged the independent 
networks together in our own CERNET.

00:01:47.538 --> 00:01:51.371
In the 1980′s, islands of similar 
networks speaking different dialects

00:01:51.413 --> 00:01:53.746
sprung up all over
Europe and the States,

00:01:53.788 --> 00:01:56.538
making remote access
possible but torturous.

00:01:56.788 --> 00:01:59.204
To make it easy for our
physicists across the world

00:01:59.246 --> 00:02:03.579
to access the ever-expanding big data
stored at CERN without traveling,